    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1867-a1">

                <pb facs="1378" n="1262" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1262"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Price to
                            Panaman Foreign Office.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 220.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-09-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 6, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to refer to my
                    note No. 186 of June 10 last in the case of the late William T. Harrington.</p>
                <p>On yesterday five years had elapsed since the death of this citizen of my
                    country.</p>
                <p>Convinced of the correctness of its position in this matter, and having exhibited
                    a consideration and patience best illustrated by the record itself herein, the
                    representations and demand of said note are repeated and made a part hereof, and
                    respectfully but emphatically I must solicit the settlement by your excellency’s
                    Government of this claim without further delay.</p>
                <p>I avail [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. Jennings Price.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
